think After ALES5 (the sample clock) landed and pushed, no custody gate was in reach — the recur continues on agent-doable Lotus work. ALES5's road-on named three: track table, crossfade curve, transport.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the track table is the most durable — the mix master a transport plays and a curve crossfades between. Chose it as ALES6, self-approved the design round.
think Designed lotus/track.rye: Track (a Clip placed at at_ms), Session (bounded ≤ max_tracks), add_track (SessionFull), render (sum every track at its clock-converted offset). The one correctness beyond a per-track add: saturate ONCE over the true sum, via a wide i64 accumulator per sample clamped once — three mid-range tracks clip as an audio editor owes, never per-track.
think The table generalizes the two proven rungs: empty renders silence, one track reproduces ALES5 place_at, two at offset zero reproduce ALES3 mix. Each offset converts through clock.samples_for; the clamp reuses timeline.saturate.
